The invention relates to a method for producing and deburring toothings on workpieces (6), utilizing two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10). In this method, the workpieces (6) are automatically clamped into the workpiece spindles (3, 3′), toothed by means of the hobbing tool (12), and subsequently deburred. The method comprises the following steps:

a. receiving an unmachined workpiece (6) at a first loading position (19) by means of a first workpiece spindle (3) and conveying the workpiece (6) to the hobbing tool (12);

b. performing a milling cut;

c. depositing the workpiece (6) at the first loading position (19) and receiving a further unmachined workpiece (6);

d. transporting the milled workpiece (6) to the second loading position (19′);

e. receiving the workpiece (6) at the second loading position (19′) by means of the second workpiece spindle (3′) and conveying the workpiece (6) to the deburring tool (10);

f. deburring the workpiece (6).

An intermediate storage (14) for at least one workpiece (6) is provided between the first loading position (19) and the second loading position (19′), whereby the workpiece (6) is transferred from the intermediate storage (14) to the second loading position (19′). Furthermore, method steps e. and f. are performed within the same time interval as method step b.

